  "notes": "5 sessions a week, 109 sets in total.\n\n## Muscle Focus\n\nSets per week. *Effective* counts each set where the muscle assists as half a set.\n\n### High priority\n\n- **Lats / upper back:** 17 sets (23 effective)\n- **Lateral delts:** 12 sets\n- **Rear delts:** 6 sets (10.5 effective)\n\n### Medium–high priority\n\n- **Glute max:** 6 sets (16 effective)\n- **Glute medius:** 6 sets (7 effective)\n\n### Moderate priority\n\n- **Quads:** 13 sets\n- **Hamstrings:** 11 sets (17 effective)\n- **Biceps:** 8 sets (16.5 effective)\n- **Triceps:** 8 sets (12 effective)\n- **Chest:** 8 sets\n- **Abs:** 8 sets\n- **Calves:** 6 sets\n\n### Indirect only\n\n- **Front delts:** no direct sets (4 effective from pressing)\n\n## Progression\n\n- **Add reps first.** Work within each exercise's rep range. When every set reaches the top of the range, add weight and drop back to the bottom.\n- **Effort.** End most sets 0–3 reps short of failure. Isolation work (lateral raises, curls, leg extensions) can go closer; keep heavy squats and Romanian deadlifts further away.\n\n### Rep ranges\n\n- **Primary lifts:** 3 × 6–10. Upper days: bench press, chest-supported row, lat pulldown. Lower days: hip thrust, back squat, Romanian deadlift.\n- **Other upper and lower day work:** 3 × 10–15\n- **Full Body day:** 2 × 10–15\n- **Lateral raises:** 4 × 10–15, every day"
